# `Symbol.for("text")` finds the one symbol that is registered under the text, wherever the call stands and however often it runs. The front end names the field of `[kState]: ..` by the text,
# Link lets the symbol go along with its key as it does for a symbol that is made once, and an access under it is an access under a name. A text that nobody knows stays a call and an access under a key.
# RUN: link accesses mechanisms=all
# CHECK: access f1 v15 under Symbol.for("registered.state")
# CHECK: access f3 v3 under Symbol.for("registered.state")
# CHECK: access f5 v6 under Symbol.for("registered.state")
# RUN(NONE): link accesses mechanisms=all
# NONE-NOT: access f4
# RUN(STORE): walk f5 mechanisms=-Inlining
# STORE-LABEL: code f5:Body
# STORE: PutSlotOrAdd {{*}}key=Symbol.for("registered.state") {{*}}orderWordAfter=
# RUN(LOOP): walk f1 mechanisms=-Inlining
# LOOP-LABEL: code f1:Body
# LOOP-NOT: CallBuiltin
# LOOP: = GetSlotOrUndefined {{*}}key=Symbol.for("registered.state")
# RUN(UNKNOWN): walk f4 mechanisms=-Inlining
# UNKNOWN-LABEL: code f4:Body
# UNKNOWN: = CallBuiltin {{*}}overload=SymbolFor
# UNKNOWN: = ElemGet
